  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Given that $\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}=b$ and $\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}=c,$ what is $b-c?$",
  "worked_solution": "We wish to subtract the following fractions:\n\n$$\nb-c=\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}\n$$\n\nIn order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $n-2$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{(-1)}{(-1)}\\cdot \\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{-2n+1}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(5n+3)-(-2n+1)}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3+2n-1}{n-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{7n+2}{n-2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
